        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best generator cover?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most open-frame portable generators, the GenTent Universal Open Frame tent is the best running cover: it clamps to the frame, uses NFPA 701-rated vinyl and lists 70 mph wind and 18-inch snow ratings. Inverter owners should choose the GenTent Inverter tent. For storage between outages, a fitted cover such as Champion&#39;s 4,800 to 11,500-watt storage cover is enough.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you run a generator with a cover on it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Only with a cover designed as a running cover or generator tent, which leaves the sides open for airflow and exhaust. Never run a generator under a storage cover, tarp or bag, which traps heat and blocks vents. The generator must still be outdoors, at least 20 feet from the house, with the exhaust pointed away from windows and doors.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is it safe to run a generator in the rain under a tent?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is safer than running it unprotected, because a running tent keeps water off the outlets and control panel. The generator must still be outdoors on raised ground, out of standing water, with dry hands on plugs and switches. Never move it into a garage, carport or under a porch roof to get it out of the rain.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I run a generator in my garage with the door open?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. An open garage door does not clear carbon monoxide, which can build up to dangerous levels within minutes and seep into the house. The CDC advises running portable generators outdoors only, at least 20 feet from the home. Put battery-powered CO alarms inside the house, and never use a generator tent as a reason to run it indoors.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How do I know what size generator cover to buy?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Check whether your generator is open frame or an enclosed inverter first, because they need different covers. Then measure the frame perimeter, length plus width doubled, without wheels and handles, and compare it to the maker&#39;s fit range or fit-finder tool. Use the wattage range on a listing only as a first filter.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do generator tents work in snow?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                GenTent-built tents, including Champion&#39;s Storm Shield, and the Westinghouse WGenTent list an 18-inch snow rating. Brush heavy wet snow off during long storms anyway, so the canopy does not sag toward the hot engine, and keep snow cleared from the exhaust outlet and the air intake so the generator can breathe freely.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I cover my generator when it is not in use?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, once it has cooled completely. A fitted storage cover keeps dust, pollen, UV and moisture away from the air intake, outlets and fuel cap, which helps the generator start reliably at the next outage. Store it in a dry place away from flames, and follow the manual for fuel and battery care over long breaks.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
